  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Virginia received $92.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 23.6% year over year. Contracting activity in Virginia includes 329,463 awards with an average award size of $280K. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry by obligations, with $29.4B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buying agency, obligating $32.8B, followed by the Department of Defense at $32.6B. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. is the largest vendor, receiving $19.9B in obligations, and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is the second largest vendor with $9.5B. Recent fiscal-year totals show obligations of $77.9B in FY21, $89.4B in FY22, $106B in FY23, $110B in FY24, $121B in FY25, and $92.1B in FY26. The data reflect contract obligations only, and current-year totals are partial because totals are fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have federal contract obligations in Virginia changed over time?",
        "body": "Fiscal-year totals show a multi-year increase through FY25, then a decline into FY26. FY21 obligations were $77.9B, FY22 obligations were $89.4B, FY23 obligations were $106B, FY24 obligations were $110B, FY25 obligations were $121B, and FY26 obligations were $92.1B. Obligations fell 23.6% year over year. The FY26 totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors account for the largest share of Virginia contracts?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buyer with $32.8B, followed closely by the Department of Defense with $32.6B. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. is the top vendor with $19.9B, followed by TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP with $9.5B. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry with $29.4B, and Computer Systems Design Services is second with $9.6B."
      }
    ]
  },
